# 📜 Custom Project Rules for ChaosChronicle

## 1. Git Rule
- **STRICT REQUIREMENT**: Never execute `git commit` or `git push` automatically.
- **EXPLICIT COMMAND ONLY**: Commits and pushes must ONLY be done when explicitly ordered by the user.

## 2. Test Execution Rule
- **STRICT REQUIREMENT**: Never run tests (e.g. `npm test`, `run_all_tests.js`, test scripts) automatically in the background.
- **EXPLICIT MANUAL REQUEST ONLY**: Automated test suites must ONLY be executed when the user explicitly instructs to run tests (e.g. "teste das Programm", "führe Tests aus").

## 3. Code Modularization Rule
- **STRICT REQUIREMENT**: All files in the codebase must remain strictly under 400 lines of code.

## 4. Build Rule
- **STRICT REQUIREMENT**: Do not run `vite build` or production bundling unless explicitly ordered. Keep Vite in development server mode.

## 5. Code Editing Rule
- **STRICT REQUIREMENT**: When making code changes, NEVER overwrite or rewrite entire files. ALWAYS make targeted edits (diffs / surgical modifications or insertions) using `replace_file_content` or `multi_replace_file_content` targeting only the specific lines.

## 6. Video Subscription Banner Rule
- **STRICT REQUIREMENT**: Every generated news video (`video.mp4`) must ALWAYS automatically include the transparent subscription animation banner (`assets/banner/sub_animation_transparent.mov`) at second 30 (0:30–0:36) using FFmpeg 30 FPS overlay.
